Social Security benefits go up 3.6% in 2027, the cost-of-living adjustment (COLA) the [Social Security Administration (SSA)](https://www.ssa.gov/cola/) announced on October 14, 2026. The average retired-worker benefit rises by roughly $75 a month, to about $2,170, starting with January 2027 payments. Supplemental Security Income (SSI) recipients see the increase starting December 31, 2026. On a $2,000 monthly benefit, 3.6% adds $72 a month, or $864 a year.